course: dictionary
lesson: 12563
title: Completely opposite
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are big, but their job is simple. Diametrically means completely, as different as two things can be. «Their views on the new park were diametrically opposed.» Look at the clues: they disagree totally. The word tells you how much they disagree.
explain: The word looks hard, but you can break it into parts. You may know diameter from maths: a straight line across a circle that goes through its centre. Diametrically comes from diameter, so it is about things lying straight across from each other.
explain: «The two dots were diametrically opposite on the circle.» Think of a clock face, with one dot at 12 and one at 6. They are exactly halfway round, with the centre between them. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The two dots were completely opposite on the circle» still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Diametrically means completely, as different as two things can be.
fact: You often see it in the phrases «diametrically opposed» and «diametrically opposite».
fact: In maths, «diametrically opposite» points are at the two ends of a diameter.
fact: A diameter is a straight line through the centre of a circle, from one edge to the other.
fact: Diametrically comes from the word diameter.
exercise: «Her ideas were diametrically opposed to mine.» What does diametrically mean here? | Politely | *Completely | Slightly | Quickly
exercise: «The two points were diametrically opposite on the circle.» Where are the points? | Tucked into one small corner | *Straight across from each other, through the centre | Outside the circle | Next to each other on the edge
exercise: «They gave diametrically opposite answers.» Find and copy the one word that means completely. | gave | answers | they | *diametrically
test: «The twins had diametrically different tastes: one loved sprouts and the other hated them.» What does diametrically mean? | Loudly | *Completely | Sometimes | A little
test: On a circle, which two points are diametrically opposite? | 9 and 10 on a clock face | 12 and 1 on a clock face | *12 and 6 on a clock face | 3 and 4 on a clock face
exam: Maya says, «Our plans are diametrically opposed.» What is she telling you? | The plans are the same, with no differences at all | The plans are small and quite hard to see | The plans are slightly similar, but a bit different | *The plans are completely different, and they disagree totally
